Grammar

Rule 0     S' -> E
Rule 1     E -> E PLUS T
Rule 2     E -> E MINUS T
Rule 3     E -> T
Rule 4     T -> NUMBER

Terminals, with rules where they appear

MINUS                : 2
NUMBER               : 4
PLUS                 : 1
error                : 

Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

E                    : 1 2 0
T                    : 1 2 3

Parsing method: LALR

state 0

    (0) S' -> . E
    (1) E -> . E PLUS T
    (2) E -> . E MINUS T
    (3) E -> . T
    (4) T -> . NUMBER

    NUMBER          shift and go to state 3

    E                              shift and go to state 1
    T                              shift and go to state 2

state 1

    (0) S' -> E .
    (1) E -> E . PLUS T
    (2) E -> E . MINUS T

    PLUS            shift and go to state 4
    MINUS           shift and go to state 5


state 2

    (3) E -> T .

    PLUS            reduce using rule 3 (E -> T .)
    MINUS           reduce using rule 3 (E -> T .)
    $end            reduce using rule 3 (E -> T .)


state 3

    (4) T -> NUMBER .

    PLUS            reduce using rule 4 (T -> NUMBER .)
    MINUS           reduce using rule 4 (T -> NUMBER .)
    $end            reduce using rule 4 (T -> NUMBER .)


state 4

    (1) E -> E PLUS . T
    (4) T -> . NUMBER

    NUMBER          shift and go to state 3

    T                              shift and go to state 6

state 5

    (2) E -> E MINUS . T
    (4) T -> . NUMBER

    NUMBER          shift and go to state 3

    T                              shift and go to state 7

state 6

    (1) E -> E PLUS T .

    PLUS            reduce using rule 1 (E -> E PLUS T .)
    MINUS           reduce using rule 1 (E -> E PLUS T .)
    $end            reduce using rule 1 (E -> E PLUS T .)


state 7

    (2) E -> E MINUS T .

    PLUS            reduce using rule 2 (E -> E MINUS T .)
    MINUS           reduce using rule 2 (E -> E MINUS T .)
    $end            reduce using rule 2 (E -> E MINUS T .)

